WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:13.514
- Seeing your son in
such a dangerous position,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:16.850
obviously, any parent
would fight

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.310
to protect their kid
at all costs.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:25.317
(police sirens)

00:00:27.569 --> 00:00:30.113
- "Defending Jacob" tells
the story of a prosecutor

00:00:30.197 --> 00:00:31.949
whose 14-year-old son is charged

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:33.617
with the murder
of a classmate.

00:00:34.451 --> 00:00:35.953
- We have some bad news.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:40.165
The print we lifted from
the victim's sweatshirt...

00:00:40.249 --> 00:00:41.667
is from your son.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.377
- Wait-- What?

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.506
- It's tricky when you're trying
to create a mini-series

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:51.802
'cause you wanna make sure each episode
has a strong engine and a purpose.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.971
- There's gotta be an explanation.

00:00:54.888 --> 00:00:57.015
- I didn't do it. I swear.

00:00:57.766 --> 00:00:59.893
- We begin to see this family tested,

00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:02.563
and she begins to
question everything.

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:04.940
- Do you have any doubts
about Jacob's innocence?

00:01:05.023 --> 00:01:06.733
- No, of course not.

00:01:06.817 --> 00:01:09.361
- It's all about the family,
how they experience it.

00:01:09.945 --> 00:01:11.405
- The foundation is rocked.

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:13.282
There's a lot of trust issues,
a lot of guilt.

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:15.576
It kind of opens
all those doors.

00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:17.411
(thunder crashes)

00:01:17.494 --> 00:01:21.290
- Is there a part of you...
thinks he might've done it?

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:23.876
- How well can you ever know anyone?

00:01:23.959 --> 00:01:26.003
And I think this show
forces us to think about

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:28.630
those boundaries that exist
with the people we love.

00:01:30.507 --> 00:01:32.926
- Once you open Pandora's box

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.721
it's those scary corners
you don't want to explore.

00:01:36.972 --> 00:01:39.183
- The twists and turns of the thriller
are fantastic,

00:01:39.266 --> 00:01:42.811
but it's this crisis of
parenting that makes it unique.

00:01:43.854 --> 00:01:46.440
- What are you willing to do
as a family?

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:48.692
How well do we know
our children?

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.694
How far are we willing to go?

00:01:50.777 --> 00:01:52.779
- The interesting thing about
this show

00:01:52.863 --> 00:01:55.073
is that it's not shot
as a TV show,

00:01:55.157 --> 00:01:57.034
it's shot like an 8-hour movie.

00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:00.370
- I know you think you know Jacob,
but you don't.

00:02:01.205 --> 00:02:02.331
- Did he do this?

00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:03.999
There's a cliffhanger every episode.

00:02:06.877 --> 00:02:08.128
- I can't find a move.

00:02:08.212 --> 00:02:09.463
- It's because you don't have one.

00:02:13.008 --> 00:02:14.927
- Jacob. How's he doing?
Whoa, whoa!

00:02:15.010 --> 00:02:15.844
- You think this is a joke?

00:02:17.179 --> 00:02:18.514
- I can't play this game anymore.

00:02:18.597 --> 00:02:19.765
- Did you do it?

